===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|stork}}, from {{inh|en|ang|storc}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*stork}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*sturkaz}}, from {{inh|en|ine-pro|*sr̥ǵos||stork}}. Near cognates include {{cog|nl|stork}}, {{cog|de|Storch}}, {{cog|sv|stork}}, and {{cog|is|storkur}}. Compare also {{ncog|lv|stārķis|t=stork}}, borrowed from Germanic.

===Pronunciation===
* {{enPR|stôrk|a=GenAm}}, {{IPA|en|/stɔɹk/}}
* {{IPA|en|/stɔːk/|a=RP}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-stork.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɔː(ɹ)k|s=1}}
* {{homophones|en|stalk|aa=non-rhotic}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q28507}}A large [[wade|wading]] [[bird]] with long legs and a long [[beak]] of the order {{taxfmt|Ciconiiformes|order}} and its family {{taxfmt|Ciconiidae|family}}.
# {{lb|en|folklore|or|euphemism}} The mythical bringer of babies to families, or good news.
#: {{ux|en|My sister's expecting a visit from the '''stork'''.}}
# {{lb|en|cartomancy}} The seventeenth [[Lenormand]] card.

